            "description": "This contract has already been awarded (2019/S 202-491600) following an OPEN process under PCR 2015.   Due to technical issues with FTS, it is not possible to link any modification notices to the original notices.   This award notice is setting out the modification to the contract .  \nThis is a Provider Selection Regime (PSR) contract modification notice. This contract has been modified under Regulation 13(1)(a) Health Care Services (Provider Selection Regime) Regulations 2023 as the modification is clearly and unambiguously provided for in the contract documents.\nFor the avoidance of doubt, the provisions of the Public Contracts Regulations 2015 do not apply to this modification. This contract has now been formally modified.\nModifications:\n1st March 2026 - 31st March 2026 - One-off uplift to the Community Detoxification offer for a sum of £37,677 to strengthen and expand the community detox pathway outline in the Service Specification.\n1st April 2026 to 31st March 2027 - Additional funding to support the continuation of drug and alcohol prevention, treatment and recovery provision across Sunderland at an additional cost of £1,975,800.48 (the National Drug and Alcohol Funding arrangements have changed and now form part of the Public Health Grant under a ringfenced drug and alcohol allocation).  This provides a basis for the maintaining and developing treatment and recovery capacity across Sunderland.\n1st July 2026 - 30th June 2028 - To utilise the optional 2 x 12 month contract extension and extend the contract from 1st July 2026 to 30th June 2028 with a total cost of £6,996,944 (equivalent to an annual value of £3,498,472 for contract years 1st July 2026 - 30th June 2027 and 1st July 2027 - 30th June 2028).",
